<title>NORWAY: STATOIL'S NORFRA GASLINE ALMOST COMPLETE.</title>
<headline>STATOIL'S NORFRA GASLINE ALMOST COMPLETE.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Laying of the southern section of the NorFra gas trunkline from the Dutch continental shelf to Dunkerque in northern France was completed on August 11, operator Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The northern section of the trunkline from the North Sea riser platform, Draupner E, to the Dutch sector is due to be finished in late August or early September, Statoil's Status Weekly newsletter said.</p>
<p>Statoil said only 90 km of the 840-km pipeline remained to be laid. When completed it will be the world's largest submarine gas pipeline.</p>
<p>--Tanya Pang, Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
